challenges.description:
What is the difference between `private` and `protected` in TypeScript?

  class Base {
    private secret = 'hidden'
    protected shared = 'visible to subclasses'
  }

  class Child extends Base {
    reveal() { return this.shared }  // ← does this work?
  }

What does `readonly` do on a class property, and when can it be set?

  class Service {
    readonly id: string
    constructor(id: string) { this.id = id }
  }

  const s = new Service('abc')
  s.id = 'xyz'  // ← what happens?

What is the difference?

  interface Logger { log(msg: string): void }
  class Base { start() { return true } }

  class App extends Base implements Logger {
    log(msg: string) { console.log(msg) }
  }

What is an abstract class and what makes it different from an interface?

  abstract class BaseChecker {
    abstract check(): Promise<boolean>
    async run(): Promise<string> {
      const ok = await this.check()
      return ok ? 'healthy' : 'unhealthy'
    }
  }
